    "Microsoft.VSTS.Common.AcceptanceCriteria": "<div><b>Acceptance Criteria</b> </div><ul><li><b>Create</b><ul><li>A user must be able to create a new report template as either a Standard Report or a One Line Summary Report, or create a new folder, within a selected folder. </li><li>Creating a template must prompt for a name before it is added to the folder's list. </li> </ul> </li><li><b>Rename</b><ul><li>A user must be able to rename an existing template or folder. </li> </ul> </li><li><b>Delete</b><ul><li>A user must be able to delete an existing template or folder, subject to a confirmation step before the deletion is applied. This story does not need to define what happens to a template's existing usages elsewhere (Project/Regime links, scratchpad/result set reports); that is owned by the features that consume templates. </li> </ul> </li> </ul>",
